{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Amazing Grace appeals to me because the familiar hymn could offer the warm, reflective feeling I enjoy in Christmas music.",
    "Some of these suggestions seem to recognize that comforting, inspirational listening might appeal to me, although only Amazing Grace gives me enough reason to try it now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Country hits and chart collections do not connect clearly enough with the Christmas albums I repeatedly chose to make me want to listen today.",
    "An inspirational title or a promise of relaxation is not enough by itself; Joey+Rory Inspired and the classical compilation leave me uncertain that they offer the particular feeling I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The suggestions seem to stretch my interest in warm, reflective music into a broader interest in country and inspirational albums.",
    "Familiar hits seem to be treated as appealing in themselves, but familiarity matters to me here when it connects with a song or mood I already want."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Christmas album choices suggest that the seasonal feeling mattered, rather than just a general preference for gentle music.",
    "Those Christmas choices happened close together, while The New Old Fashioned came much later; I would not assume they all reflect the same listening occasion or that I am seeking Christmas music every time."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions partly capture a comforting, reflective mood but extend it too broadly into albums that give me little specific reason to listen."
}"}
